    <div class="prose">
      <p>A fitted wardrobe isn't something a homeowner urgently needs, it's something they see and fall for. The awkward alcove that finally makes sense, the clutter gone, the bedroom that suddenly looks like a hotel. Nobody's typing "emergency wardrobe" into Google. They get sold on it when they see a beautiful one done well. That's exactly what a good ad does.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <p>I target homeowners, and the ads are built around the jobs worth having:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Fitted and bespoke wardrobes</li>
        <li>Sliding-door wardrobes</li>
        <li>Awkward alcove and under-stairs storage</li>
        <li>Full fitted bedrooms</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="split">
        <div class="prose" style="margin:0;">
          <h2>Why footage wins this trade</h2>
          <p>Because it's a want, not a need, the homeowner has to <em>see</em> it to want it. A photo doesn't do a fitted wardrobe justice, but footage panning across a finished run of sliding doors, or an awkward alcove turned into proper storage, sells it instantly. So we use <strong>real footage of your builds</strong>, filmed on site or from work you've already done, never stock. The finish is the sell.</p>
